      "firstSeen": "2026-05-14T00:00:00.000Z",
      "files": [
        {
          "path": "SKILL.md",
          "contents": "# Frontend design\n\nAnswer three questions before writing any component: what the product is, who reads it, and which single tradeoff this screen makes. Name the tradeoff out loud. Then pick one type scale, one spacing scale, and one accent color, and write them down before markup.\n\nReject the template look: centered hero, three equal cards, purple gradient. If the brief genuinely calls for that, say why. Otherwise the layout has to be earned by the content.\n\nWhen reviewing your own work, list what you avoided deciding. That list is usually longer than the design notes, and it is where the redesign starts.\n\nChecklist before shipping a screen:\n- the primary action is visually unambiguous\n- body text is at least 15px and line length 60-80 characters\n- every interactive element has a visible focus state\n- no color carries meaning alone\n"
        },
        {
          "path": "references/type-scales.md",
          "contents": "Modular scales: 1.125, 1.2, 1.25, 1.333, 1.5."
        },
        {
          "path": "references/layout-patterns.md",
          "contents": "Split, stacked, overlaid, and asymmetric two-column patterns."
        }
      ]
    },
    "101-skills/superpowers/ai-video-generation": {
      "id": "101-skills/superpowers/ai-video-generation",
      "source": "101-skills/superpowers",
      "slug": "ai-video-generation",
      "hash": "1c2d3e4f5a6b7c8d9e0f1a2b3c4d5e6f7a8b9c0d1e2f3a4b5c6d7e8f9a0b1c2d",
      "description": "Generate AI videos from still images and text prompts.",
      "weeklyInstalls": [
        23000,
        25000,
        26000,
        26000,
        40000,
        43000,
        45000,
        48100
      ],
      "firstSeen": "2026-04-21T00:00:00.000Z",
      "files": [
        {
          "path": "SKILL.md",
          "contents": "# AI video generation\n\nTurn a still image or a short prompt into a video clip. Pick a provider, write the prompt, submit, then verify the clip before reporting success.\n\nWorkflow:\n1. Ask what the clip is for (ad, explainer, social) and how long it should be. Duration drives provider choice more than quality does.\n2. Write the prompt as scene, subject, motion, camera, then style. Keep motion to one verb.\n3. Submit the job and poll until it leaves the queue. Do not invent a job id.\n4. When the file lands, check duration, resolution and that the subject is still on screen at the end.\n5. Save the finished clip next to the source prompt so the run can be repeated.\n\nCosts and failure modes:\n- Most providers bill per second of output; a 30s retry is not free.\n- Text rendering inside generated video is still unreliable. If the clip needs legible words, composite them afterwards.\n- Faces hold up for a few seconds, then drift. Cut before the drift.\n"
        },
        {
          "path": "references/providers.md",
          "contents": "Provider matrix: model, max duration, aspect ratios, per-second price."
        },
        {
          "path": "references/prompt-patterns.md",
          "contents": "Prompt skeletons for product shots, b-roll, and character motion."
        },
        {
          "path": "scripts/poll-job.sh",
          "contents": "#!/usr/bin/env bash\nset -euo pipefail\necho poll\n"
        }
      ]
    },
    "anthropics/skills/pdf": {
